@startuml
hide footbox
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
title Plain console: one complete line at a time

participant "KeyboardWarrior" as main <<class>>
participant "reader:BufferedReader" as reader
participant "machine:StateMachine" as machine
participant "current:State" as state

note over main, state
  Scope: runPlainGame(...) after initial-state setup.
  All shown calls execute on the main thread.
  The input-handling example retains the current state.
end note
loop while running
  main -> reader : readLine()
  reader --> main : line
  alt line is null (EOF)
    main -> machine : stop()
    machine --> main
  else complete input line
    main -> machine : handleInput(line)
    machine -> state : handleInput(line)
    state --> machine
    machine --> main
  end
end
note over main, state
  No periodic StateMachine.update() call runs here.
  Enter delivers the typed text; evaluation uses its actual elapsed time.
  Output and shutdown internals are omitted.
end note
@enduml
